income volatility"}], "description": "Why it matters: The creator economy often blends entrepreneurship with instability and unpaid platform work."}, {"id": "c992b6e5-09c9-4f8d-83df-1c75b720c418", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Rights and ownership", "children": [{"id": "5d08ae3d-7dba-4b15-8245-a98429ee0951", "type": "concept", "title": "copyright"}, {"id": "c2bc8b94-728a-467a-a527-e1b964b6828b", "type": "concept", "title": "licensing"}, {"id": "a27ef997-4b5c-4031-b039-9868d028be0a", "type": "concept", "title": "work-for-hire"}, {"id": "0618ac97-fce2-4214-b73c-fe83407cb5a8", "type": "concept", "title": "collective bargaining"}], "description": "Why it matters: Students study intellectual property, contracts, platform terms, and bargaining power."}]}, {"id": "de62a9b0-cbe3-4e21-a5d5-2e13ba75a36b", "type": "topic", "title": "Globalization of Media, Platforms, and Technology Markets", "description": "Communication technologies operate across borders, but regulation, culture, language, and geopolitics vary. Students analyze global platform power and transnational media flows.", "children": [{"id": "a1835cb2-d179-4efc-8a58-856e91acadfe", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Global media markets", "children": [{"id": "d6e46bb7-076f-4e89-8d05-4f5899e0c18c", "type": "concept", "title": "format trade"}, {"id": "ad74b067-ea1f-4477-ba1a-0be90fd7a23d", "type": "concept", "title": "localization"}, {"id": "d8f89528-0820-4317-8563-0485a8b14681", "type": "concept", "title": "global streaming"}, {"id": "94d512eb-cb7a-4cf9-a132-fb62a94a8cee", "type": "concept", "title": "soft power"}], "description": "Why it matters: Students study how content travels through formats, franchises, streaming platforms, and cultural adaptation."}, {"id": "40a9c956-cc98-429f-9883-413fa7a4a60b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Platform geopolitics", "children": [{"id": "50343a72-8070-4a91-9590-df36be2168af", "type": "concept", "title": "data sovereignty"}, {"id": "6e26b220-abda-4589-a0c2-c8ca064d158d", "type": "concept", "title": "content takedowns"}, {"id": "8f338792-4d30-4db2-9b9b-bad0fd367ad5", "type": "concept", "title": "platform bans"}, {"id": "0031067e-7e78-40e0-9d2d-e68704ed8d3c", "type": "concept", "title": "digital trade"}], "description": "Why it matters: Technology firms face state regulation, data localization, censorship, and trade conflict."}, {"id": "59985d07-b041-481d-b1fc-a3c3ba5abae1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Unequal global access", "children": [{"id": "de7a578c-7e30-47ed-8766-89498271b119", "type": "concept", "title": "connectivity gaps"}, {"id": "26ccbf35-e302-442f-b2e0-68cb3bb2ef1a", "type": "concept", "title": "outsourced moderation"}, {"id": "46ad2174-0503-4631-ae2a-d5e593974524", "type": "concept", "title": "language markets"}, {"id": "0534744f-3a67-4a3c-a399-818dc7a211af", "type": "concept", "title": "cultural imperialism"}], "description": "Why it matters: Global communication markets reproduce inequalities in infrastructure, language, labor, and representation."}]}, {"id": "9513e953-7a78-4422-bbf0-235539d7ffc1", "type": "topic", "title": "Communication Policy, Regulation, and Governance", "description": "Policy sets the rules for competition, speech, privacy, infrastructure, and public-interest obligations. Students learn to evaluate policy choices as communication design.", "children": [{"id": "75c1d51d-a979-4583-b047-95d8795a4197", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Regulatory institutions", "children": [{"id": "0066c77f-035a-4c5b-a10e-b06a859d553d", "type": "concept", "title": "FCC"}, {"id": "42360de3-7235-40cc-9e2c-ec6e2c2e283b", "type": "concept", "title": "FTC"}, {"id": "988f31b7-e03c-41f0-a9af-a78ccd87cd9d", "type": "concept", "title": "courts"}, {"id": "5f30b93c-4763-4804-9a99-598559980a83", "type": "concept", "title": "EU regulators"}, {"id": "e33da5e1-a6b1-424f-941e-ab52690a55eb", "type": "concept", "title": "standards bodies"}], "description": "Why it matters: Students learn the roles of agencies, courts, legislatures, and international